 in Bristol Photography", "creditUrl": "https://www.pexels.com/photo/a-person-in-black-long-sleeves-holding-a-tray-with-glasses-of-champagne-13375022/", "url": "https://cdn.recurxive.com/packs/spanish-vocabulary/images/pair-el-camarero.webp"}, "shape": "pair", "speak": {"text": "El mesero", "lang": "es-419"}, "uid": "1ds2nma1p6nwpi"}, {"id": "pair-la-carta", "tags": ["food-drink"], "sideA": {"modality": "text", "value": "El menú"}, "sideB": {"modality": "text", "value": "The menu"}, "illustration": {"imagePrompt": "A large leather-bound restaurant menu", "imageSearchTerm": "restaurant menu leather", "alt": "Restaurant menu leather"}, "shape": "pair", "speak": {"text": "El menú", "lang": "es-419"}, "uid": "12c3b821iirp4u"}, {"id": "pair-la-propina", "tags": ["food-drink"], "sideA": {"modality": "text", "value": "La propina"}, "sideB": {"modality": "text", "value": "The tip"}, "illustration": {"imagePrompt": "A few loose coins on a tablecloth", "imageSearchTerm": "coins tip table", "alt": "Coins tip table"}, "shape": "pair", "speak": {"text": "La propina", "lang": "es-419"}, "uid": "qgpmmfe1pqkt"}, {"id": "pair-quisiera", "tags": ["food-drink"], "sideA": {"modality": "text", "value": "Quisiera..."}, "sideB": {"modality": "text", "value": "I would like..."}, "illustration": {"imagePrompt": "A customer pointing at a menu item politely", "imageSearchTerm": "customer menu polite", "alt": "Customer menu polite", "credit": "Pexels · Rachel Claire", "creditUrl": "https://www.pexels.com/photo/bar-counter-in-close-up-5863642/", "url": "https://cdn.recurxive.com/packs/spanish-vocabulary/images/pair-quisiera.webp"}, "shape": "pair", "speak": {"text": "Quisiera", "lang": "es-419"}, "uid": "8ihlfp3coph7"}, {"id": "fact-buen-provecho", "tags": ["food-drink", "culture"], "title": "The Meaning of Buen Provecho", "body": "It is common courtesy to say **Buen provecho** (*Enjoy your meal*) when food is served or when walking past people who are eating. It fosters a communal, social atmosphere.", "shape": "fact", "illustration": {"imageSearchTerm": "restaurant diners sharing meal", "imagePrompt": "People at a lively restaurant enjoying a meal together at their tables.", "alt": "The Meaning of Buen Provecho", "depictable": true, "credit": "Pexels · Gera Cejas", "creditUrl": "https://www.pexels.com/photo/two-women-having-a-lunch-together-20400372/", "url": "https://cdn.recurxive.com/packs/spanish-vocabulary/images/fact-buen-provecho.webp"}, "speak": {"text": "Buen provecho", "lang": "es-419"}, "uid": "1137hm91ng6a6n"}, {"id": "mcq-ordering-phrase", "tags": ["food-drink"], "options": [{"modality": "text", "value": "Yo quiero pollo."}, {"modality": "text", "value": "¿Hay pollo esta noche?"}, {"modality": "text", "value": "Dame el pollo."}, {"modality": "text", "value": "Para mí, el pollo."}], "correctIndex": 3, "explanation": "'Para mí...' is the natural, casual way to state your order when the waiter is going around the table.", "shape": "mcq", "prompt": {"modality": "text", "value": "The waiter is going around the table taking orders. Which is the natural, casual way to state your order for the chicken?"}, "speak": {"text": "Para mí, el pollo", "lang": "es-419"}, "uid": "4oaboa8kadjm"}, {"id": "ih-paella-valenciana", "shape": "fact", "tags": ["food-drink"], "factVariant": "image-heavy", "title": "Paella valenciana", "body": "Saffron rice with rabbit, chicken, and beans — a classic dish of Valencia.", "illustration": {"imagePrompt": "A wide traditional paella pan filled with saffron rice, rabbit, chicken, and beans.", "imageSearchTerm": "paella valenciana saffron rice", "alt": "A wide pan of traditional Spanish paella with saffron rice", "kind": "photo", "depictable": true}, "imageCaption": "Valencia's dish — and the traditional version has rabbit, not seafood.", "speak": {"text": "Paella valenciana", "lang": "es-419"}, "uid": "1pneyq9joc5y"}, {"id": "cz-spanish-vocabulary-ih-paella-valenciana", "shape": "cloze", "tags": ["food-drink"], "template": "Saffron ___ with rabbit, chicken, and beans — a classic dish of Valencia.", "answer": "rice", "distractors": ["olive oil", "vegetables", "bread"], "derivedFrom": "ih-paella-valenciana", "explanation": "Paella is built on rice (arroz), colored and flavored with saffron.", "speak": {"text": "Arroz", "lang": "es-419"}, "uid": "4g1n2o1thyqec"}, {"id": "mcq-c-spanish-vocabulary-ih-paella-valenciana", "shape": "mcq", "tags": ["food-drink"], "prompt": {"modality": "text", "value": "Saffron ___ with rabbit, chicken, and beans — a classic dish of Valencia."}, "options": [{"modality": "text", "value": "bread"}, {"modality": "text", "value": "vegetables"}, {"modality": "text", "value": "olive oil"}, {"modality": "text", "value": "rice"}], "correctIndex": 3, "explanation": "Paella is built on rice (arroz), colored and flavored with saffron.", "derivedFrom": "ih-paella-valenciana", "speak": {"text": "Arroz", "lang": "es-419"}, "uid": "jacdrytcn8om"}, {"id": "tf-t-spanish-vocabulary-pair-la-cuenta", "shape": "trueFalse", "tags": ["food-drink"], "statement": "\"La cuenta\" means \"The bill / check\".", "isTrue": true, "why": "La cuenta means The bill / check.", "derivedFrom": "pair-la-cuenta", "speak": {"text": "La cuenta", "lang": "es-419"}, "uid": "jo3dz910klkzr"}, {"id": "tf-t-spanish-vocabulary-pair-el-camarero", "shape": "trueFalse", "tags": ["food-drink"], "statement": "\"El mesero\" means \"The waiter\".", "isTrue": true, "why": "El mesero means The waiter.", "derivedFrom": "pair-el-camarero", "speak": {"text": "El mesero", "lang": "es-419"}, "uid": "61q2fglbhipo"}, {"id": "tf-f-spanish-vocabulary-pair-la-carta", "shape": "trueFalse", "tags": ["food-drink"], "statement": "\"El menú\" means \"The waiter\".", "isTrue": false, "why": "El menú actually means The menu.", "derivedFrom": "pair-la-carta", "speak": {"text": "El menú", "lang": "es-419"}, "uid": "m0h4861iz8jxq"}, {"id": "tf-f-spanish-vocabulary-pair-la-propina", "shape": "trueFalse", "tags": ["food-drink"], "statement": "\"La propina\" means \"I would like...\".", "isTrue": false, "why": "La propina actually means The tip.", "derivedFrom": "pair-la-propina", "speak": {"text": "La propina", "lang": "es-419"}, "uid": "grr02xzywlw3"}, {"id": "tf-f-spanish-vocabulary-pair-quisiera", "shape": "trueFalse", "tags": ["food-drink"], "statement": "\"Quisiera...\" means \"The waiter\".", "isTrue": false, "why": "Quisiera... actually means I would like....", "derivedFrom": "pair-quisiera", "speak": {"text": "Quisiera", "lang": "es-419"}, "uid": "38nhlmhknupi"}, {"id": "ot-carta-meaning", "shape": "mcq", "tags": ["restaurant", "menu"], "prompt": {"modality": "text", "value": "In a restaurant, what does 'el menú' refer to?"}, "options": [{"modality": "text", "value": "The bill at the end"}, {"modality": "text", "value": "The waiter's tip"}, {"modality": "text", "value": "The reservation you made"}, {"modality": "text", "value": "The menu you order from"}], "correctIndex": 3, "explanation": "'El menú' is the menu you order from, and 'la carta' means the same thing. In Spain, 'el menú' usually means the fixed-price set meal (menú del día) rather than the full list of dishes.", "source": {"label": "Spanish Vocabulary — Objective Test"}, "speak": {"text": "el menú", "lang": "es-419"}, "uid": "6xwmemghllsu"}, {"id": "ot-ask-bill", "shape": "mcq", "tags": ["restaurant", "bill"], "prompt": {"modality": "text", "value": "When you're ready to pay, what do you say to ask for the check?"}, "options": [{"modality": "text", "value": "La propina, por favor"}, {"modality": "text", "value": "Buen provecho"}, {"modality": "text", "value": "El menú, por favor"}, {"modality": "text", "value": "La cuenta, por favor"}], "correctIndex": 3, "explanation": "'La cuenta, por favor' asks for the bill. 'El menú' is the menu and 'la propina' is the tip.", "source": {"label": "Spanish Vocabulary — Objective Test"}, "speak": {"text": "La cuenta, por favor", "lang": "es-419"}, "uid": "1bqaeygin4gus"}, {"id": "ot-propina-meaning", "shape": "mcq", "tags": ["restaurant", "tip"], "prompt": {"modality": "text", "value": "What does 'la propina' mean?"}, "options": [{"modality": "text", "value": "The bill"}, {"modality": "text", "value": "The menu"}, {"modality": "text", "value": "The tip"}, {"modality": "text", "value": "The waiter"}], "correctIndex": 2, "explanation": "'La propina' is the tip. In Mexico it is voluntary: a restaurant may not add it to the bill without your consent.", "source": {"label": "Spanish Vocabulary — Objective Test"}, "speak": {"text": "la propina", "lang": "es-419"}, "uid": "qhest31fpo9n1"}, {"id": "ot-waiter-latam", "shape": "mcq", "tags": ["restaurant", "waiter", "regional"], "prompt": {"modality": "text", "value": "What word for 'the waiter' is common in most of Latin America?"}, "options": [{"modality": "text", "value": "El gerente"}, {"modality": "text", "value": "El mesero"}, {"modality": "text", "value": "El dependiente"}, {"modality": "text", "value": "El cocinero"}], "correctIndex": 1, "explanation": "'El mesero' is the usual Latin American word (in Spain: 'camarero'). 'Gerente' is manager, 'cocinero' is cook, 'dependiente' is shop clerk.", "source": {"label": "Spanish Vocabulary — Objective Test"}, "speak": {"text": "El mesero", "lang": "es-419"}, "uid": "x4odvxbpzcqj"}, {"id": "ot-paella-region", "shape": "mcq", "tags": ["paella", "regional"], "prompt": {"modality": "text", "value": "Paella is most closely associated with which region of Spain?"}, "options": [{"modality": "text", "value": "Valencia"}, {"modality": "text", "value": "Andalusia"}, {"modality": "text", "value": "Galicia"}, {"modality": "text", "value": "Catalonia"}], "correctIndex": 0, "explanation": "Paella is Valencia's signature dish. It originated in the Valencian Community.", "source": {"label": "Spanish Vocabulary — Objective Test"}, "uid": "dtrgb51ky5u03"}, {"id": "ot-paella-base", "shape": "mcq", "tags": ["paella", "rice"], "prompt": {"modality": "text", "value": "Paella valenciana combines rabbit, chicken, and beans over what base?"}, "options": [{"modality": "text", "value": "Fresh egg noodles"}, {"modality": "text", "value": "Potatoes"}, {"modality": "text", "value": "Saffron rice"}, {"modality": "text", "value": "Bread"}], "correctIndex": 2, "explanation": "Paella is built on rice (arroz), colored and flavored with saffron.", "source": {"label": "Spanish Vocabulary — Objective Test"}, "speak": {"text": "Paella valenciana", "lang": "es-419"}, "uid": "iraffp16d18jv"}, {"id": "ot-paella-not-ingredient", "shape": "mcq", "tags": ["paella", "ingredients"], "prompt": {"modality": "text", "value": "Which is NOT a traditional ingredient of paella valenciana?"}, "options": [{"modality": "text", "value": "Rabbit"}, {"modality": "text", "value": "Fish"}, {"modality": "text", "value": "Chicken"}, {"modality": "text", "value": "Beans"}], "correctIndex": 1, "explanation": "Paella valenciana uses rabbit, chicken, and beans over saffron rice; fish is not part of the traditional Valencian version.", "source": {"label": "Spanish Vocabulary — Objective Test"}, "speak": {"text": "paella valenciana", "lang": "es-419"}, "uid": "1l0bovw17lgnsc"}, {"id": "fact-carta-not-menu", "tags": ["food-drink", "restaurant", "false-friends"], "title": "El menú vs la carta", "body": "**El menú** is the list of dishes you order from, and **la carta** means the same thing. In Spain, **el menú** usually means something else: the **menú del día**, a fixed-price set meal and one of the better deals at lunch. Order from the menu with *Quisiera...*, or — casually, as the waiter works around the table — *Para mí, el pollo*.", "shape": "fact", "illustration": {"imageSearchTerm": "menú del día restaurante", "imagePrompt": "A chalkboard outside a restaurant in Spain listing the fixed-price menú del día in Spanish.", "alt": "A chalkboard headed 'Menu del dia' lists first and second courses to choose from, handwritten in Spanish, with set prices in euros.", "depictable": true, "credit": "Centenoyespelta · CC BY-SA 4.0", "creditUrl": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Menu_del_dia_Aupa.jpg", "subject": "A wooden-framed chalkboard headed 'Menu del dia' listing first and second courses in Spanish and set prices in euros, under a 'Basque Wine' sign.", "url": "https://cdn.recurxive.com/packs/spanish-food-shopping/images/fact-carta-not-menu.336fa7af.webp"}, "speak": {"text": "El menú", "lang": "es-419"}, "uid": "1fgac8phpfiif"}, {"id": "fi-mcq-ordering-phrase", "tags": ["food-drink"], "title": "Para mí, el pollo", "body": "When a waiter goes around the table, 'Para mí, el pollo' ('For me, the chicken') is the natural, polite way to state your order.", "shape": "fact", "illustration": {"imageSearchTerm": "roast chicken restaurant plate", "imagePrompt": "A waiter setting down a plate of roast chicken in front of a diner at a restaurant table.", "alt": "Para mí, el pollo", "depictable": true, "credit": "Pexels · Nishant Aneja", "creditUrl": "https://www.pexels.com/photo/cooked-food-on-plate-2494648/", "url": "https://cdn.recurxive.com/packs/spanish-vocabulary/images/fi-mcq-ordering-phrase.webp"}, "speak": {"text": "Para mí, el pollo", "lang": "es-419"}, "uid": "sd5a6rrgvrpt"}, {"id": "fi-ot-ask-bill", "tags": ["restaurant", "bill"], "title": "La cuenta, por favor", "body": "In Spain, servers don't bring the check automatically, so diners ask for it with 'la cuenta, por favor.'", "shape": "fact", "illustration": {"imageSearchTerm": "waiter bringing restaurant bill", "imagePrompt": "A waiter placing a small bill folder on a restaurant table for the diners.", "alt": "La cuenta, por favor", "depictable": true, "credit": "Pexels · Vitaly Gariev", "creditUrl": "https://www.pexels.com/photo/people-in-a-restaurant-23496892/", "url": "https://cdn.recurxive.com/packs/spanish-vocabulary/images/fi-ot-ask-bill.webp"}, "speak": {"text": "La cuenta, por favor", "lang": "es-419"}, "uid": "5tarfr10bdud"}]}